    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A medieval Bulgarian state restored by the revolt of Peter and Asen in 1185 and ruled from the fortress of Tsarevets in Tarnovo.</li><li>Kaloyan destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> crusaders at Adrianople in 1205, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ivan-asen-ii">Ivan Asen II</a> dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#balkans">Balkans</a> after Klokotnitsa in 1230.</li><li>Its Tarnovo literary school shaped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Slavic culture before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> took Tarnovo in 1393 and Vidin in 1396.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>After his capture at Adrianople in 1205, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#latin">Latin</a> emperor Baldwin I was held at Tarnovo; a tower of the Tsarevets fortress is still known as Baldwin's Tower.</p></aside>
    </section>

